We are grateful to all OFCs for a good feedback on the weekly Multi-origin =
report.

Please find the WK46 PFMC Vs. R/vol(Reference vol) by OFC & customer as att=
ached.
All loading OFCs under 70%(in green) are kindly required to send reasons by=
 Wednesday(Nov 20th).
RHQ Contract managers & HO are also requested to pay keen attention to reas=
ons loading
OFCs get you.

We know that some customers have already headed into their slow season but =
TPE PFMC of
several customers such as Pantos, W/Mart, LG Sourcing, Goodyear & TOY "R" U=
S falls
short of their average TPE vols for last 10 weeks(R/vol), so all concerning=
 contract & loading PIC
are kindly requested to come up with reasons and take measures unless you a=
nticipate any upswing
in near time.
For further details on their PFMC, please refer to # in green/boldface on t=
he tap " WK46 PFMC
by ACCT " in the attachment.

FYR, please refer to notes below for the attachment.

 - The purpose of this report is to enhence the communication among loading=
 & contract OFCs/RHQs.
 - R/Vol : not target but reference vols based on average Vol for last 10 w=
eeks.
 - OFCs with PFMC ratio under 70%(Vs. R/Vol) are only supposed to be shown =
in green.

Thanks & B. RGDS

